- 12-table persistence contract and reversible migration `20260809_0021`;
- protected persisted-data-only APIs for people, person detail and organization map;
- Next.js Professional Context list/detail/organization-map workspace through a server-only control-plane client;
- three governed professional-context source candidate families, all unauthorized/unscheduled/non-executable with no runtime adapter, approved hosts or approved paths;
- router composition and canonical navigation integration;
- architecture boundaries prohibiting network/browser/platform automation, collection orchestration, opportunity and outreach dependencies;
- README, roadmap and Lot 21 release/validation documentation synchronized to `0.22.0` and Lot 22 next.

## Explicitly not added

- no active scanning or probing;
- no browser automation;
- no authenticated LinkedIn or Discord automation;
- no private messages, friend graphs, personal addresses or private-life profile data;
- no credential handling;
- no automatic need/opportunity creation;
- no outreach authorization or sending path.

LinkedIn, Discord, BrixHub and other account/licence-dependent integrations remain Lot 22 and require provider-specific positive approval dossiers before execution.

