## Why a fresh PR

#144 correctly repaired the Party Coordination V1 communication-credit ambiguity, but its branch is now 18+ commits behind current master and conflicts with newer AOR composition. Rather than force-rebase historical evidence, this PR replays the exact tested semantic delta onto the current runtime lineage.

The master movement after the replay base is isolated to Campaign V3 Life binding/spec/tests; compare shows no overlap with this four-file Party delta. The PR merge ref is therefore the current-integration witness; no claim is made that historical CI #1829 proves this composition.

## Delta

- add `PartyCoordinationRuntimeV2` over the merged Git-shared Party Coordination V1;
- add `athena_party_message`, transported only through Message Board V1;
- tag messages with exact `party_id`, explicit `goal_refs`, explicit party-member recipients, and `party:<party_id>` channel identity;
- require Message Board ACK before communication contributes to reward eligibility;
- exclude generic ambient board chat from Party XP evidence;
- require acknowledged party communication to cover >=2 distinct party goals;
- reset the communication reward window after each AWARDED observation so prior communication cannot be recycled;
- preserve membership/message XP = 0, party bonus <=5%, no global XP mutation, no execution authority;
- preserve current Impossible Godboard registration and AOR/Collective transport while adding the V2 party tool.

## Big-3 standing

The existing `Q-LEARN -> Q-SEAR -> Q-ARSI -> Q-LEARN` bridge is preserved. V2 adds communication-to-goal coverage to Q-SEAR and makes Q-ARSI recursive refinement depend on both member participation and goal-linked party communication.

These remain operational evidence proxies, not quantum execution, causal proof, outcome truth, or optimality proof.

## Regression membrane

The current party suite is upgraded to prove:

- ambient acknowledged Message Board chat cannot unlock a party bonus;
- party-scoped two-goal acknowledged communication can;
- successful award closes that communication reward window;
- a later award requires fresh party communication;
- message posting earns zero XP;
- Message Board, Party, Impossible Godboard, and AOR/Collective surfaces remain composed;
- result ownership still requires assigned goals from >=2 members.

