## Scope

This Draft PR semantically replays the minimum reusable material-engineering foundation from the heavily diverged E001 collision branch onto current `main`.

It intentionally does **not** carry collision, tunneling, response-motion, runtime LUT/codegen, or general relation-algebra work. Those remain on their owning lines.

## What changed

- adds finite integer material curve transforms (`H_p`, `G_p`, loading/return profile observables);
- adds the bounded root-basin/versine real-data fitter;
- separates experimental measurement scale/unit metadata from model precision `A`;
- introduces a fixed benchmark domain so train/test splitting cannot silently redefine the material coordinate system;
- adds deterministic train-only fitting and five-fold held-out validation;
- preserves the Treloar data/source lineage and explicit prior-art boundary;
- adds all-points and held-out Treloar benchmark scripts;
- adds bilingual validation-gate documentation and regression tests.

## Why

The previous all-points Treloar result demonstrated representation capacity but not generalization. It also left experimental quantization scale and finite model precision too easy to conflate.

This PR makes the engineering gate explicit:

`declared measurement scale -> fixed benchmark domain -> train-only calibration -> held-out evaluation`

Higher precision may open additional fitting freedom, but it must earn that freedom on held-out data rather than being promoted solely because training SSE falls.

## Current benchmark boundary

On the deterministic interleaved five-fold Treloar split (fixed domain `[100,761]`), independently reconstructed RMSE values are approximately:

- Neo-Hooke: `0.7999`
- Mooney-Rivlin: `0.6351`
- Yeoh-2: `0.3142`
- Yeoh-3: `0.1244`
- E001 integer `A=128`: `0.2145`
- E001 integer `A=2048`: `0.1842`
- E001 integer `A=8192`: `0.1804`

So the finite integer family is nontrivial, but it **does not beat Yeoh-3** on held-out Treloar uniaxial data. That negative boundary is part of the acceptance evidence.

## Validation added

Regression tests cover:

- integer transform scale/order properties;
- fixed Treloar reference fits;
- exact measurement-scale rational representation;
- explicit separation of observation scale and `A`;
- held-out target leakage (changing a test target must not alter the fitted training model);
- deterministic five-fold Treloar aggregate/per-fold errors;
- fixed-domain and evaluation-shape validation.

The branch is currently based directly on current `main` with no behind commits at PR creation. Repository-wide CI should be judged from GitHub checks on this PR; no pre-creation full-repository CI claim is made.

