## Summary

Implement the first headless AR-08 lighting slice tracked by #41 inside `@greenways/alumbra-engine`.

```text
canonical Core chunks + block light metadata
        ↓
deterministic loaded-set propagation
        ↓
private sunlight and emitted-light arrays
        ↓
immutable per-chunk field views
        ↓
generation / epoch / revision-fenced installation
```

## Lighting contracts

This adds closed Engine formats for:

- `alumbra.lighting-profile/1`;
- `alumbra.light-field/1`;
- `alumbra.light-field-set/1`;
- lighting jobs, invalidation evidence, installation receipts and runtime evidence.

Profiles bound values to `0–15`, require positive attenuation and choose one explicit missing-neighbour policy:

- `opaque`: missing vertical chunk segments block sunlight below the highest loaded segment;
- `open`: every loaded top face without a loaded `+Y` neighbour is exposed sky.

## Block metadata

Lighting reads canonical block definitions through:

```text
metadata.light.opacity
metadata.light.emission
```

The existing `lightOpacity` and `emittedLight` names remain accepted aliases. Conflicting, unknown or out-of-range lighting declarations fail before a field is returned.

Empty blocks and blocks with `render.opaque = false` transmit by default; other blocks are fully opaque unless they declare a bounded opacity.

## Deterministic propagation

- sunlight is seeded from the exact loaded sky boundary;
- emitted light is seeded from block sources;
- both propagate through six-neighbour voxel adjacency;
- every step attenuates by at least one;
- level buckets are processed from high to low with stable numeric node ordering;
- input chunk order and queue insertion order cannot alter the result;
- propagation crosses loaded chunk boundaries, including negative coordinates;
- no light field is invented for an unloaded chunk.

The build is bounded to 4,096 chunks and 16,777,216 loaded voxels.

## Hot field boundary

Dense `Uint8Array` values remain private inside Engine field views. Public consumers receive point sampling, explicit copies and bounded evidence only.

Dense light fields are not placed in:

- Hara values;
- Hodos models;
- history checkpoints;
- content-addressed archive cells;
- renderer resources.

## Runtime and stale-result fencing

A lighting job captures:

- the newest requested generation;
- the current runtime epoch;
- the exact sorted loaded chunk set and revisions;
- the complete normalized lighting profile.

Installation rejects profile drift, old generations, changed chunk revisions or changed epochs. A late worker result cannot replace current fields.

Updating one chunk invalidates only loaded chunks whose nearest voxel lies within the maximum propagation radius. Unrelated distant fields remain readable until the next field set is installed. Disposal clears chunks, fields and invalidation state and reports an exact baseline.

## Tests

Focused Engine tests cover:

- closed profile validation;
- vertical sunlight attenuation;
- contiguous and missing vertical chunk segments;
- open-sky versus opaque-gap policy;
- deterministic emitted-light propagation;
- negative-coordinate cross-chunk propagation;
- opaque barriers;
- malformed block metadata;
- bounded invalidation radius;
- preservation of unaffected fields;
- stale revision, generation and epoch rejection;
- idempotent zero-resource disposal.

## Authority boundary

The implementation depends only on `@greenways/alumbra-core`. It imports no DOM, browser storage, filesystem/network service, PlayCanvas, Hodos, Hara rule implementation, History Store, Hestia, Ignatius or Tahto code.

This PR deliberately stops before renderer mesh attributes or Catalog stories. Those can follow once the headless field and fencing contract is green.

