## Goal

Make the completion proof ledger inspectable without running fresh verification or mutating Goal state.

## Read-only `/goal audit`

- add strict no-argument `/goal audit` parsing;
- report Goal/session IDs, status/revision/storage generation, execution binding, usage/budget, progress and stop/blocker state;
- for unfinished Goals, explain the existing `auditCompletion()` result as `READY` or `NOT READY` with exact gate reasons;
- for completed Goals, report `COMPLETED` plus the persisted completion summary instead of incorrectly re-entering the pre-completion gate;
- expose every requirement with status/source/verification mode and evidence references;
- expose evidence trust/kind/pass state/revision/timestamp/source/summary without dumping arbitrary metadata or re-running commands/verifiers;
- mark stale-revision evidence explicitly;
- state explicitly that the report is a read-only snapshot.

## Ownership safety

The audit wrapper reuses the lower read-only `/goal status` command path only to seed command ownership, then translates the visible response. Binding the visible audit response therefore cannot be mistaken for user intervention and cannot pause or rewrite the live Goal.

